### Why

The V8 downloader fetched the checksum manifest on every package build. Two GitHub connection resets therefore stopped `co build` even though the local manifest, archive and binding already matched the repository trust pin.

### Goal

Make verified V8 caches usable offline and make incomplete cache downloads resilient without weakening the repository-pinned trust boundary.

### Accomplished

- Authenticate the cached manifest and both artifacts before any network access.
- Download missing or corrupt entries into unique sibling temporary files and replace formal cache files only after validation.
- Preserve existing formal files on failures and clean temporary files.
- Retry reset, timeout, 408/429/5xx and downloaded checksum failures at most three times with injectable exponential backoff; reject deterministic HTTP failures immediately.
- Add regressions for offline hits, reset/checksum recovery, preservation/cleanup, retry bounds and HTTP classification.
- Document the V8 cache merge protection in `docs/pacth`.
- Validation: V8 tests 10/10, codex_package tests 27/27 and `git diff --check` passed.
